Git & GitHub DevOps Command Reference Cheat Sheet
Comprehensive Markdown README reference containing setup, workflows, and line-by-line explanations for DevOps engineering.
Quick Copy & Paste Reference
Below is a single consolidated script format containing all standard DevOps Git operations in sequential order:
# ==========================================
# GIT & GITHUB DEVOPS COMPLETE REFERENCE
# ==========================================
# 1. INITIAL SETUP & CONFIGURATION
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com"
git config --global init.defaultBranch main
git config --global core.editor "vim"
git config --global core.autocrlf input
# 2. REPOSITORY INITIALIZATION & CLONING
git init
git clone git@github.com:org/repo.git
git clone -b dev git@github.com:org/repo.git
git clone --depth 1 git@github.com:org/repo.git
# 3. STAGING, COMMITTING & HISTORY
git status
git add .
git commit -m "feat: add dockerfile for microservice"
git commit --amend --no-edit
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all
# 4. BRANCHING & REBASE STRATEGIES
git branch -a
git switch -c feature/jira-1234
git switch main
git merge feature/jira-1234
git rebase main
git branch -d feature/jira-1234
# 5. REMOTE SYNC & UPSTREAM
git remote -v
git remote add upstream git@github.com:original-org/repo.git
git fetch origin
git pull --rebase origin main
git push -u origin feature/jira-1234
git push origin --delete feature/jira-1234
# 6. UNDOING CHANGES & TROUBLESHOOTING
git restore --staged filename.txt
git restore filename.txt
git stash
git stash pop
git revert <commit-hash>
git reset --soft HEAD~1
# 7. TAGGING & RELEASES
git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "Release version 1.0.0"
git push origin v1.0.0
# 8. GITHUB CLI AUTOMATION
gh pr create --title "feat: pipeline update" --body "Added helm deployment steps"

gh release create v1.0.0 --generate-notes
gh workflow run deploy-prod.yml
Detailed Command Breakdown & Justification
Command Why & When We Use It
git config --global

Sets author identity and environment defaults globally across all local repos. Essential for
tracking commit ownership in audit logs.

git clone --depth 1

Performs a shallow clone fetching only the latest commit. Reduces pipeline build times and
network bandwidth in CI/CD runners.

git commit --amend --no-edit

Appends staged changes to the previous commit without changing the message. Cleanly
updates PRs without clogging history with minor fixes.

git log --oneline --graph

Renders a concise, visual branch topology in terminal to inspect merge histories and active
development branches.

git rebase main

Applies local commits on top of updated upstream main branch, maintaining a clean, linear git
history before merging pull requests.

git pull --rebase

Fetches remote commits and replays unpushed local work over them, avoiding cluttering git
history with unnecessary merge commits.

git revert <hash>

Generates a new commit that safely reverses changes from a specified commit. Ideal and safe
for production branch rollback.

git reset --soft HEAD~1

Undoes the last commit while keeping modified files staged, allowing commits to be
restructured or rephrased before pushing.

git tag -a v1.0.0

Creates a cryptographically signed/annotated release tag. Used by deployment tools (ArgoCD,
Jenkins) to trigger image builds and releases.

gh workflow run

Triggers GitHub Actions workflows directly from CLI/terminal without logging into the web
interface.
